<section class="faq-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How do I know if my rash is serious?</h3>
            <p>Seek immediate care if your rash is accompanied by fever, difficulty breathing, rapid spreading, or signs of infection. Most rashes aren't emergencies, but persistent or worsening symptoms warrant a dermatology evaluation.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Can melasma be cured?</h3>
            <p>While melasma can be challenging to treat, it can be significantly improved with consistent use of topical lightening agents, chemical peels, and strict sun protection. Maintenance therapy is often needed.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How long does it take for skin discoloration to fade?</h3>
            <p>This varies depending on the cause and depth of pigmentation. Superficial discoloration may improve in weeks to months, while deeper pigmentation may take 6-12 months or longer with treatment.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
